WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.056
Priya: Okay, the duty contact list is current. Lukas is primary on-call from this point.

2
00:00:07.056 --> 00:00:13.201
Lukas: I can open the roster and incident record. Who approves any wider routing change?

3
00:00:13.201 --> 00:00:20.809
Raj: The rostered incident coordinator owns that decision. Their paging alias is tested and recorded.

4
00:00:20.809 --> 00:00:29.426
Hannah: I'm on it for carrier communications. Ticket access works, but phone escalation needs verification.

5
00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:37.106
Anika: Raj verified the contracted support number earlier. Use the authenticated account reference in storage.

6
00:00:37.106 --> 00:00:45.122
Priya: Just to confirm, secrets stay out of chat, right? Contact references don't need copied credentials.

7
00:00:45.122 --> 00:00:51.219
Lukas: Agreed, and if I don't respond promptly? Who receives the backup page tonight?

8
00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:57.507
Raj: The roster routes it to the backup SRE. Page the backup after about five minutes.

9
00:00:57.507 --> 00:01:04.828
Hannah: The escalation path opens from my account too. We won't depend on an outgoing engineer.

10
00:01:04.828 --> 00:01:12.460
Priya: So, contact access is now confirmed. Raj remains available until final acceptance only.

